#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:5
msgid "Acer WMI Battery interface driver (acer-wmi-battery)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:8
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:10
msgid ""
"Some Acer laptops support setting battery charge control limits and allow a "
"user to calibrate their battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:14
msgid "WMI interface description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:16
msgid ""
"The WMI interface description can be decoded from the embedded binary MOF "
"(bmof) data using the `bmfdec <https://github.com/pali/bmfdec>`_ utility:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:33
msgid ""
"For all methods the ``uBatteryNo`` is always ``0x1``, there are no known "
"Acer laptop models with two batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:37
msgid "WMI method GetBatteryInfoInterface()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:39
msgid ""
"Returns additional battery information, the data seems to be based on the "
"\"Smart Battery Data Specification\". The only known value for "
"``uBatteryInfoIndex`` is ``0x8``, the battery temperature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:44
msgid "WMI method GetBatteryHealthControlStatus()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:46
msgid ""
"This interface does not exist on all Acer laptops, it returns whether "
"battery charge limiting or calibration mode is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:49
msgid ""
"When calling this method, ``uFunctionList`` is a bitmask with known values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:52
msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:52
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:54
msgid "0x01"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:54
msgid "Health mode supported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:56
msgid "0x02"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:56
msgid "Calibration mode supported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:59
msgid ""
"``uFunctionStatus`` is a 5 byte array known elements are ``0`` for health "
"mode and ``1`` for calibration mode. A non-zero value means the mode is "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:63
msgid "WMI method SetBatteryHealthControl()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:65
msgid ""
"This interface does not exist on all Acer laptops, it enables battery charge "
"limiting or battery calibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../wmi/devices/acer-wmi-battery.rst:68
msgid ""
"The argument ``uFunctionMask`` is known to accept either ``0x01`` for "
"setting health mode or ``0x02`` for calibration mode; other values are "
"unknown. ``uFunctionStatus`` is an uint8 value, a non-zero value enables the "
"given mode."
msgstr ""
